@ 2:5  di|rection LR
  2:3-2:15 "direction LR"
  | **`direction LR`** direction: left to right
  |
  | `direction TB`, `BT`, `RL` or `LR`: the direction of the diagram, or of the composite state it is in.
@ 3:5  st|ate f <<fork>>
  3:3-3:8 "state"
  | **`state`**
  |
  | `state X { … }` or `state "description" as X { … }`: a composite state; `--` splits it into concurrent regions.
@ 3:15  state f <<fo|rk>>
  3:11-3:19 "<<fork>>"
  | **`<<fork>>`**
  |
  | `state f <<fork>>`, `<<join>>`, `<<choice>>` (or `[[fork]]` …): a pseudo-state.
@ 4:15  state c [[ch|oice]]
  4:11-4:21 "[[choice]]"
  | **`[[choice]]`**
  |
  | `state f <<fork>>`, `<<join>>`, `<<choice>>` (or `[[fork]]` …): a pseudo-state.
@ 5:5  no|te left of A : text
  5:3-5:7 "note"
  | **`note`**
  |
  | `note left of A : text`, or `note right of A`, the text on the lines after it, then `end note`. A floating `note "text" as N` is accepted and not drawn.
@ 8:5  en|d note
  8:3-8:11 "end note"
  | **`end note`**
  |
  | `note left of A : text`, or `note right of A`, the text on the lines after it, then `end note`. A floating `note "text" as N` is accepted and not drawn.
@ 9:5  cl|assDef x fill:#f00
  9:3-9:11 "classDef"
  | **`classDef`**
  |
  | `classDef name fill:#f96,color:#000`: defines a class of styles.
@ 11:8  A -|-> B
  11:7-11:10 "-->"
  | **`-->`** transition `A` → `B`
  |
  | `A --> B`: a transition.
@ 12:6  -|-
  12:5-12:7 "--"
  | **`--`**
  |
  | `--` splits a composite state into concurrent regions.
@ 15:5  A:|::x
  15:4-15:7 ":::"
  | **`:::`**
  |
  | `A:::name`: gives the state a class, as `class A name` does.
@ 16:5  hi|de empty description
  16:3-16:25 "hide empty description"
  | **`hide empty description`**
  |
  | `hide empty description`: accepted and ignored.
@ 17:5  st|yle A fill:#bbf
  17:3-17:8 "style"
  | **`style`**
  |
  | `style A,B fill:#f96`: styles states.
